{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "nr-pleasure-craft-state",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.5 step 7e: the `nr-pleasure-craft-state` RunSpec computed from the DEFAULT DATABASE -- the whole of Florida, August 2020, weekday, the Pleasure Craft sector, gasoline: outboards, inboard/sterndrives and personal water craft, 30 points over 3 SCCs, 110 cohorts, 440 rows.\n\nIT SELECTS SEVEN POLLUTANT-PROCESSES AND NONROAD EMITS FOUR. The other three are benzene (20) at processes 22, 23 and 24 -- permeation -- which `runspecpollutantprocess` carries and no exhaust slot produces, so MOVESOutput has no row for them; the output relation read the SELECTED set until this run, and emitted 330 rows of zeros. It is now `n_outputPolProcess` wide, the selections whose pollutant has an output slot (moves.rs `SLOT_POLLUTANT`), declared and recomputed. The marine gasoline SCCs are 2282005 and 2282010, which the SCC-prefix table reads as 2- and 4-stroke gasoline by their SEVEN-digit prefix. All 440 rows reproduce at 6.923e-06."
  },
